    "summary": "The University of Edinburgh offers flexible study abroad options including Study Abroad Programme, International Exchange, Erasmus exchange, Parliamentary Programme, and Summer School courses. Students can choose to study for one semester or the full academic year.",
    "strengths": [
      "The university has a strong international student support system with dedicated Visiting Student Advisers, well-established exchange programs, and diverse academic offerings. It provides structured support for visiting students including course selection assistance, accommodation arrangements, and academic guidance."
    ],
    "facilities": [
      "The university offers extensive facilities including modern gyms with various classes (yoga, boxing, zumba, dance), sports facilities (swimming pool, squash, fencing, basketball, climbing), and student societies. Accommodation options include both catered and self-catered residences with facilities like common rooms and fitness centers."
    ],
    "student_life": [
      "Student life includes vibrant social activities, flat parties, and opportunities to join various clubs and societies. The university has an International Student Center offering trips and volunteer opportunities. There are also cultural experiences like Scottish traditional dance groups and Highland tours. The city offers free museums and art galleries, and innovative learning weeks provide travel opportunities within Europe."
    ]
  },
