    "exchange_type": "International Exchange",
    "application_process": "Apply via online application system; select Visiting Student Category as 'Coming as a Nominated Exchange Student' and 'International Exchange'; complete course selection; submit application by deadline; receive email with MyEd portal registration instructions; upload supporting documents (Academic Transcript, English language certificate if required) within a month after application deadline; contact relevant Visiting Student Office (CAHSSvisitingstudents@ed.ac.uk or SCEvisitingstudents@ed.ac.uk) for questions",
    "course_registration_notes": "All students are required to take 60 University of Edinburgh credits per semester. Select a maximum of 100 course credits per semester in case your first choices are not available (standard semester credit load is 60 credits). [Source: https://edwebcontent.ed.ac.uk/sites/default/files/atoms/files/23.24_pgn_virginia_1.pdf]\n\nYou will NOT receive an email containing a link to complete your application at this stage. This will happen later in Step 9. If you couldn't add your preferred courses, you can fill in the Course Ranking form and attach it to your application (on any blank field) instead. [Source: https://edwebcontent.ed.ac.uk/sites/default/files/atoms/files/23.24_pgn_virginia_1.pdf]\n\nCourse Finder on the Study Abroad website may be displaying courses offered in the previous academic year and so you may find there are differences between the courses listed there and those available to select in your online application. If the course offering changes after you have submitted your online application the Visiting Student Office will be in contact to advise you. [Source: https://edwebcontent.ed.ac.uk/sites/default/files/atoms/files/23.24_pgn_virginia_1.pdf]\n\nYou may also wish to use PATH to help you build a timetable and see which courses fit together. HOWEVER please note that not all courses shown on PATH are available to visiting students – this is only to be used as a timetabling tool. Timetables for 2026/27 will be updated on PATH closer to the start of the semester. [Source: https://edwebcontent.ed.ac.uk/sites/default/files/atoms/files/23.24_pgn_virginia_1.pdf]",
    "additional_requirements": {
      "extracted_notes": [
        {
          "requirement": "You must take the majority of your classes (40 out of 60) credits in the College of your choice – please keep this in mind when ranking your selection.",
